<!doctype html><html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1"><title>LVDC review worksheet</title><style>@font-face{font-family:Lato;src:url(lato2-regular.woff)}@font-face{font-family:Lato;src:url(lato2-bold.woff);font-weight:700}*{box-sizing:border-box}body{font:18px/1.6 Lato,Arial,sans-serif;color:#34383c;background:#f3f5f8;margin:0}header{background:#24265f;color:white;padding:32px max(24px,calc((100vw - 1000px)/2))}header img{width:150px;height:60px;object-fit:contain;object-position:left}h1{font-size:36px;line-height:1.18;margin:20px 0 14px}h2{font-size:25px;color:#343895;line-height:1.3}h3{font-size:20px}main{max-width:1050px;margin:36px auto;padding:0 24px 50px}article,section.card{background:white;border:1px solid #dbe1e8;border-radius:14px;padding:28px;margin:24px 0}a{color:#343895;text-underline-offset:3px}a:hover{color:#527b20}p{margin:12px 0}nav{display:flex;gap:15px;flex-wrap:wrap;margin:18px 0}.badge{background:#8DC63F;color:#192048;border-radius:50px;padding:5px 12px;font-size:13px;font-weight:700;display:inline-block}table{border-collapse:collapse;width:100%;margin:20px 0}th,td{padding:12px;border:1px solid #cbd1d9;text-align:left;vertical-align:top}th{background:#eef2f7}li{margin:9px 0}.answer{min-height:95px;border:1px solid #aeb9c6;border-radius:5px;padding:12px;white-space:pre-wrap}.muted{color:#69727d;font-size:15px}button,.button{background:#343895;color:white;border:0;border-radius:7px;padding:10px 17px;font:inherit;text-decoration:none;cursor:pointer}button:focus-visible,a:focus-visible,[contenteditable]:focus-visible{outline:3px solid #8DC63F;outline-offset:4px}.compact{font-size:16px}@media(max-width:600px){body{font-size:16px}h1{font-size:29px}article,section.card{padding:20px}th,td{padding:8px;font-size:14px}table{display:block;overflow:auto}}@media print{header{background:white;color:#343895;padding:0}header img,nav,button{display:none}body{background:white;font-size:11pt}main{max-width:none;margin:0;padding:0}article,section.card{break-inside:avoid;border:0;padding:0;margin:22px 0}.answer{min-height:90px}h1{font-size:22pt}}</style></head><body><header><img src="../ocp_academy_white.svg" alt="OCP Academy"><h1>LVDC review worksheet</h1><p>Turn each module into a specific interface question and evidence request</p></header><main><p>Use the prompts with a proposed architecture, or with the fictional review case in Module 10. Record assumptions separately from evidence. Allow about 4–6 minutes per module for reflection and reference reading if using the full three-hour learning plan.</p><p class="muted">Entries stay in this browser on this device. They are not sent to the LMS or a server. Save a print/PDF copy if you need a portable record.</p><nav><button id="print">Print / save PDF</button><button id="clear">Clear worksheet entries</button><a href="related_training.html">Related training</a></nav><section class="card" id="module1"><span class="badge">MODULE 1</span><h2>LVDC adoption and system architecture</h2><p>Choose one failure boundary in a power-chain drawing. Can you trace a complete surviving route to the load, including the supporting services?</p><label for="answer1"><strong>Your review notes</strong></label><div class="answer" id="answer1" contenteditable="true" role="textbox" aria-multiline="true" aria-label="Module 1 review notes"></div></section><section class="card" id="module2"><span class="badge">MODULE 2</span><h2>Voltage bands and equipment compatibility</h2><p>Choose one source and one load in a proposed interface. What voltage, time, power, or earth-reference information would you request before accepting the connection?</p><label for="answer2"><strong>Your review notes</strong></label><div class="answer" id="answer2" contenteditable="true" role="textbox" aria-multiline="true" aria-label="Module 2 review notes"></div></section><section class="card" id="module3"><span class="badge">MODULE 3</span><h2>Polarity earthing and configuration choices</h2><p>Choose one conductor in a bipolar drawing. Can you identify its normal-current role and distinguish that role from the protective path?</p><label for="answer3"><strong>Your review notes</strong></label><div class="answer" id="answer3" contenteditable="true" role="textbox" aria-multiline="true" aria-label="Module 3 review notes"></div></section><section class="card" id="module4"><span class="badge">MODULE 4</span><h2>Fault behavior protection and personnel safety</h2><p>Choose one claim about a protective device. Does it describe interruption, current limitation, isolation, or verification? What evidence supports that exact function?</p><label for="answer4"><strong>Your review notes</strong></label><div class="answer" id="answer4" contenteditable="true" role="textbox" aria-multiline="true" aria-label="Module 4 review notes"></div></section><section class="card" id="module5"><span class="badge">MODULE 5</span><h2>Power conversion storage and distribution</h2><p>Choose one storage or conversion block. Which event must it support, which loads are inside its boundary, and which dependencies remain outside?</p><label for="answer5"><strong>Your review notes</strong></label><div class="answer" id="answer5" contenteditable="true" role="textbox" aria-multiline="true" aria-label="Module 5 review notes"></div></section><section class="card" id="module6"><span class="badge">MODULE 6</span><h2>The LVDC rack interface</h2><p>Choose one rack entry approach. Can you assign an owner to conversion, precharge, protection, isolation, and local energy storage?</p><label for="answer6"><strong>Your review notes</strong></label><div class="answer" id="answer6" contenteditable="true" role="textbox" aria-multiline="true" aria-label="Module 6 review notes"></div></section><section class="card" id="module7"><span class="badge">MODULE 7</span><h2>Control sequences and operation</h2><p>Choose one abnormal condition, such as failed precharge or a lost measurement. Is the next permitted action defined, and who owns that decision?</p><label for="answer7"><strong>Your review notes</strong></label><div class="answer" id="answer7" contenteditable="true" role="textbox" aria-multiline="true" aria-label="Module 7 review notes"></div></section><section class="card" id="module8"><span class="badge">MODULE 8</span><h2>EMC and system stability</h2><p>Choose one noise or control-interaction concern. Which physical path and operating state would a representative test need to include?</p><label for="answer8"><strong>Your review notes</strong></label><div class="answer" id="answer8" contenteditable="true" role="textbox" aria-multiline="true" aria-label="Module 8 review notes"></div></section><section class="card" id="module9"><span class="badge">MODULE 9</span><h2>Codes standards and verification</h2><p>Choose one requirement in a proposal. Can you identify its current status, scope, applicable edition, responsible reviewer, and supporting evidence?</p><label for="answer9"><strong>Your review notes</strong></label><div class="answer" id="answer9" contenteditable="true" role="textbox" aria-multiline="true" aria-label="Module 9 review notes"></div></section><section class="card" id="module10"><span class="badge">MODULE 10</span><h2>Integrated LVDC design review</h2><p>Choose the most consequential open item in the fictional proposal. Can you name the owner, the verification method, and the result that would close it?</p><label for="answer10"><strong>Your review notes</strong></label><div class="answer" id="answer10" contenteditable="true" role="textbox" aria-multiline="true" aria-label="Module 10 review notes"></div></section><section class="card"><h2>Evidence register</h2><p>For the integrated review, name the claim, the open question, its owner and what would close it.</p><table><thead><tr><th>Claim / assumption</th><th>Evidence needed</th><th>Owner</th><th>Acceptance / next action</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td contenteditable="true" role="textbox" aria-label="Evidence row 1, Claim" id="evidence0_0" style="height:80px"></td><td contenteditable="true" role="textbox" aria-label="Evidence row 1, Evidence" id="evidence0_1" style="height:80px"></td><td contenteditable="true" role="textbox" aria-label="Evidence row 1, Owner" id="evidence0_2" style="height:80px"></td><td contenteditable="true" role="textbox" aria-label="Evidence row 1, Acceptance" id="evidence0_3" style="height:80px"></td></tr><tr><td contenteditable="true" role="textbox" aria-label="Evidence row 2, Claim" id="evidence1_0" style="height:80px"></td><td contenteditable="true" role="textbox" aria-label="Evidence row 2, Evidence" id="evidence1_1" style="height:80px"></td><td contenteditable="true" role="textbox" aria-label="Evidence row 2, Owner" id="evidence1_2" style="height:80px"></td><td contenteditable="true" role="textbox" aria-label="Evidence row 2, Acceptance" id="evidence1_3" style="height:80px"></td></tr><tr><td contenteditable="true" role="textbox" aria-label="Evidence row 3, Claim" id="evidence2_0" style="height:80px"></td><td contenteditable="true" role="textbox" aria-label="Evidence row 3, Evidence" id="evidence2_1" style="height:80px"></td><td contenteditable="true" role="textbox" aria-label="Evidence row 3, Owner" id="evidence2_2" style="height:80px"></td><td contenteditable="true" role="textbox" aria-label="Evidence row 3, Acceptance" id="evidence2_3" style="height:80px"></td></tr><tr><td contenteditable="true" role="textbox" aria-label="Evidence row 4, Claim" id="evidence3_0" style="height:80px"></td><td contenteditable="true" role="textbox" aria-label="Evidence row 4, Evidence" id="evidence3_1" style="height:80px"></td><td contenteditable="true" role="textbox" aria-label="Evidence row 4, Owner" id="evidence3_2" style="height:80px"></td><td contenteditable="true" role="textbox" aria-label="Evidence row 4, Acceptance" id="evidence3_3" style="height:80px"></td></tr></tbody></table><p class="muted">This worksheet supports a review conversation. It does not approve an engineering design or replace the applicable project verification and acceptance process.</p></section></main><script>const fields=[...document.querySelectorAll('[contenteditable]')];for(const f of fields){try{f.textContent=localStorage.getItem('lvdc-worksheet-'+f.id)||''}catch(e){}f.addEventListener('input',()=>{try{localStorage.setItem('lvdc-worksheet-'+f.id,f.textContent)}catch(e){}})}document.querySelector('#print').addEventListener('click',()=>window.print());document.querySelector('#clear').addEventListener('click',()=>{if(confirm('Clear your worksheet entries on this device?'))for(const f of fields){f.textContent='';try{localStorage.removeItem('lvdc-worksheet-'+f.id)}catch(e){}}});</script></body></html>